{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "It's Time to Travel", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Catching up With Peter and John", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Future Forms ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to talk about current actions happening now or future arrangements. <br /><br /> subject + to be + <span class=\"italic\">verb</span> + ing <br /> Example: <br /><span class=\"italic\">I am <span class =\"strong\">applying</span> for a new job.</span> <br>   <br>You use <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span> to talk about future intentions. You use the form:<br>   <br>subject + to be + going to + <span class=\"italic\">verb </span><br> Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\"> I'm going to <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">start</span></span> applying for jobs.</span><br>  <br>You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span> tense to talk about future schedules.<br> Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\">The job <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">starts</span></span> in two weeks.</span>", "type": "describer"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Life Events", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<br>Events that happen in your life are called life events. There are names for these events. Here are a few:<br>  <span class=\"italic\"><br><ul><li>first day of school/work</li> <li>birthday</li> <li>graduation</li> <li>getting a job</li> <li>promotion</li> <li>wedding</li> <li>having a baby</li> <li>anniversary (10th/25th)</li> <li>retiring</li></ul> </span>", "type": "describer"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to graduate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get a degree from a college or university ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm graduating soon from college.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le01ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you can use to talk about key life events.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to have a blast ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have a lot of fun; a great time ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's looks like you're having a blast in Paris!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le01ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cruise ship", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large ship that people have holidays on ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I got a job on a cruise ship. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le01ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to notice ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to realize", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You won't notice we're gone.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le01ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to travel by plane", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm flying to South America next week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le01ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Congratulations! ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "use to say you are happy about something someone achieved", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Congratulations on your new job!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le01ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "aunt ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the sister of your mother or father ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She's going to visit her aunt!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le01ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "off to ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "going to ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm off to Spain!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le01ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le01ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Talk to different people. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Fill in the table below. ", "type": "text"}, {"content"